{
  "name": "HERE Tile Usage Check",
  "description": "Checks whether HERE raster tile API usage dropped after the Sept 6 cached-tile-layer fix, by reading the app's Map Tiles (HERE) usage logs for Sept 7-11 and reporting the comparison to Robert.",
  "trigger": {
    "condition": null,
    "config": {
      "trigger_type": "scheduled",
      "events": [],
      "schedule_mode": "one_time",
      "cron_expression": null,
      "one_time_date": "2026-09-11T15:00:00Z",
      "timezone": "America/Edmonton",
      "interval_value": null,
      "interval_unit": null,
      "interval_anchor": null,
      "ends_type": "never",
      "ends_on_date": null,
      "ends_after_count": null
    }
  },
  "definition": {
    "do": [
      {
        "check_tile_usage": {
          "call": "invoke_superagent_step",
          "then": "end",
          "with": {
            "message": "Scheduled follow-up (agreed with Robert on Sept 6): The HERE tile cache fix was deployed Sept 6 (commit 4a154af5b \u2014 Dashboard switched to CachedTileLayer, SW v13 caches opaque responses, accurate usage counter). Pre-fix baseline was ~2,900 real HERE raster tile hits/day (82,489 in August).\n\nPlease:\n1. Read the GoogleAPILog entity in the RxDeliver app (app_id 68570f3cd01bfa2d2408a9d6), filter api_type = 'Map Tiles (HERE)', and sum call_count per day for Sept 7-11.\n2. Compare the daily totals to the ~2,900/day pre-fix baseline.\n3. Report the results to Robert on WhatsApp, keeping it SHORT (he uses text-to-speech). Include whether usage dropped as expected, and note that devices re-fetch their tile set once after the SW v13 rollout, so the first day or two may still be elevated.\n4. If usage did NOT drop meaningfully, investigate (check whether the SW is registering on driver APK devices) before replying."
          }
        }
      }
    ],
    "document": {
      "dsl": "1.0.0",
      "name": "here_tile_usage_check",
      "namespace": "base44",
      "version": "1.0"
    }
  }
}